{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-120281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/assets/41a40c03043152177c5bf6d7f56b51c09e57352480599b508d376018d87de1b3.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a+\\mu b$, find $\\lambda $ and $\\mu .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-120281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/assets/ccc52cbcbf17db97ad3849f157b5d6ab3e10f59846e2cd4b75507fc0a37c3c98.png)\n\nIn $△OAC$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OA=3|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OA}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=-3a.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $AC=2|b|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $b$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=-2b.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =-3a-2b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a+\\mu b=-3a-2b.$ \n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =-2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-120281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f66b95477e3fd4aff005164763c9298aa032d48599f8a4ac1c88bac4f1175796"} {"question" "q-120281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-120281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =-3$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =-2$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =2$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =3$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =2$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-120281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =-2$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-278288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/assets/ba82c6b68026b0f4339c1e4fa01c4b1aa1b7aee74b74176f81bba1c0e1de259f.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=r,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OS}=s$ and $V$ divides $\\overset{―}{RS}$ in the ratio $RV:VS=6:5.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OV}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-278288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RV}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=r,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{RV}.$\n\nFirst, from $△ORS,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RS} & =\\overset{\\to }{RO}+\\overset{\\to }{OS} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{OS} \\\\  & =-r+s \\\\  & =s-r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $RV:VS=6:5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RV}=\\frac{6}{11}\\overset{\\to }{RS}=\\frac{6}{11}(s-r).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OV} & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RV} \\\\  & =r+\\frac{6}{11}(s-r) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{11}r+\\frac{6}{11}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-278288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f66b95477e3fd4aff005164763c9298aa032d48599f8a4ac1c88bac4f1175796"} {"question" "q-278288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-278288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\frac{1}{11}r+s"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\frac{5}{11}r+\\frac{6}{11}s"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\frac{5}{6}r+\\frac{1}{6}s"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\frac{6}{11}r+\\frac{5}{11}s"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OV}=r+\\frac{5}{6}s"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-278288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\frac{5}{11}r+\\frac{6}{11}s"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-322577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/assets/de33644bcad663e67dc19c687dc0ef959310a50ddb83203031e66b951700510b.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=u,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OV}=v,$ and $W$ divides $\\overset{―}{UV}$ in the ratio $UW:WV=9:8.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OW}$ via the vectors $u$ and $v.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OW}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$u+$\n{{field-2}}\n$v$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-322577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=u,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{UW}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OUV,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =\\overset{\\to }{UO}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-u+v \\\\  & =v-u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $UW:WV=9:8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{UW}=\\frac{9}{17}\\overset{\\to }{UV}=\\frac{9}{17}(v-u).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OW} & =\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\  & =u+\\frac{9}{17}(v-u) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{17}u+\\frac{9}{17}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-322577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f66b95477e3fd4aff005164763c9298aa032d48599f8a4ac1c88bac4f1175796"} {"question" "q-322577" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-322577" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{17}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-322577" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-322577" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{17}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-327078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/assets/4c1a8cde010abbeaf318a64e6c9f3b6cbd3e7bac84babbcda4c1ebfb483fa2b2.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $s=\\lambda m+\\mu n$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-327078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/assets/e018cc5b4760b578d9ca514f9de6641e823bf5f6a8e17f019ebf24fc6ccb2248.png)\n\nIn $△OTS$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OT=4|m|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OT}$ and $m$ have the opposite direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OT}=-4m.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $TS=2|n|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{TS}$ and $n$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{TS}=2n.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =\\overset{\\to }{OT}+\\overset{\\to }{TS} \\\\  & =-4m+2n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $s=\\lambda m+\\mu n=-4m+2n.$\n\nSince $m∦n,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-4$ and $\\mu =2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-327078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f66b95477e3fd4aff005164763c9298aa032d48599f8a4ac1c88bac4f1175796"} {"question" "q-327078" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-327078" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-327078" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-327078" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-367062" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/assets/5a5fcb431f6019d26cd6a92d703bfd2f9393bd494b2a3834dfb7e0f2668df393.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $c=\\lambda a+3b,$ then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-367062" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+3b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $3b.$ So, we first draw the vector $3b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/assets/43fdebc1ce180542e3cfdaf3f19e27e7ac869bbc5e37da7380886bd3d817bfb7.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $3b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =3b-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a+3b=-a+3b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-1\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-367062" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f66b95477e3fd4aff005164763c9298aa032d48599f8a4ac1c88bac4f1175796"} {"question" "q-367062" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"} {"question" "q-367062" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069110/state.json" "file_sha256" "247df6b9e9f9e008cec97914d7b5d6481fda41f26e757bc69767cedbc35d96ef"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2338 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
